## What the lift test said, and how it moved the model

**The design.** The test switched {{ tested|lower }} off in {{ v('geo.treated_geos') }} of the
{{ v('sim.geos') }} simulated geos for {{ v('geo.window_weeks') }} weeks, weeks {{ v('geo.start_week') }}
to {{ v('geo.end_week') }} of the panel (a spend change of {{ v('geo.spend_change') }}), with the other
{{ v('geo.control_geos') }} geos as controls and the {{ v('geo.pre_period_weeks') }} weeks before it as the
pre period. Geos were assigned by a stratified draw across the size distribution. Power was
estimated by simulation, {{ v('geo.power_simulations') }} runs for each candidate design; at the true
effect this design's power is {{ v('geo.power_at_true_effect') }}, and the smaller designs that were
considered are in `docs/experiments.md`. The design was hashed and registered before any of the
test's weeks were read: plan hash `{{ v('geo.plan_hash') }}`, registered at {{ v('geo.registered_at') }}.
It was registered locally in this build, in `results/experiments/registry.json`, because the build
sandbox could not reach the live API; the same design and result were replayed to the live registry
from a separate client afterwards ({{ v('geo.replay.status') }}, experiment
`{{ v('geo.replay.experiment_id') }}`, same plan hash: {{ v('geo.replay.plan_hash_matches') }}), which
`docs/serving.md` records as a replay, not a pre-registration. The sample ratio gate {{ v('geo.srm_passed') }} (p = {{ v('geo.srm_p') }}).

**The result against the truth.** Difference in differences puts the revenue the channel caused in
the treated geos over the window at {{ v('geo.did.estimate') }} ({{ v('geo.did.lower') }} to
{{ v('geo.did.upper') }}). Synthetic control, fit on the pre period, puts it at {{ v('geo.sc.estimate') }}
({{ v('geo.sc.lower') }} to {{ v('geo.sc.upper') }}){% if raw('geo.sc.p_value') == 0 %}, and none of its
{{ v('geo.sc.placebo_permutations') }} placebo assignments produced a gap as large (placebo p value
{{ v('geo.sc.p_value') }}){% else %}, with a placebo p value of {{ v('geo.sc.p_value') }} from
{{ v('geo.sc.placebo_permutations') }} permutations{% endif %}. The truth, known only because the market is
simulated, is {{ v('geo.truth') }}. The difference in differences interval
{{ 'covers' if raw('geo.did.covers_truth') == 'yes' else 'misses' }} it and the synthetic control's
{{ 'covers' if raw('geo.sc.covers_truth') == 'yes' else 'misses' }} it.
{% call m.holds(raw('geo.did.estimate') > raw('geo.truth') and raw('geo.sc.estimate') > raw('geo.truth'), 'that both lift estimates sit above the truth') %}
Both estimates sit above the truth, by {{ v('geo.did.error') }} and {{ v('geo.sc.error') }}.
{% endcall %}

{{ table('geo.estimates') }}

{{ label('geo.estimates') }}

