both mix models: in own as a pseudo observation weighted by the experiment's precision, in bayes as
a lift test measurement. On the tested channel, own's return on ad spend went from
{{ v('calibrate.own.roas_before') }} ({{ v('calibrate.own.roas_before_lower') }} to
{{ v('calibrate.own.roas_before_upper') }}) to {{ v('calibrate.own.roas_after') }}
({{ v('calibrate.own.roas_after_lower') }} to {{ v('calibrate.own.roas_after_upper') }}), and bayes's from
{{ v('calibrate.bayes.roas_before') }} ({{ v('calibrate.bayes.roas_before_lower') }} to
{{ v('calibrate.bayes.roas_before_upper') }}) to {{ v('calibrate.bayes.roas_after') }}
({{ v('calibrate.bayes.roas_after_lower') }} to {{ v('calibrate.bayes.roas_after_upper') }}). The true
return is {{ v('calibrate.own.roas_true') }}.
{% set own_closer = (raw('calibrate.own.roas_after') - raw('calibrate.own.roas_true'))|abs < (raw('calibrate.own.roas_before') - raw('calibrate.own.roas_true'))|abs %}
{% set bayes_closer = (raw('calibrate.bayes.roas_after') - raw('calibrate.bayes.roas_true'))|abs < (raw('calibrate.bayes.roas_before') - raw('calibrate.bayes.roas_true'))|abs %}
{% call m.holds(own_closer and bayes_closer and raw('calibrate.own.covers_before') == 'yes' and raw('calibrate.bayes.covers_before') == 'yes' and raw('calibrate.own.covers_after') == 'no' and raw('calibrate.bayes.covers_after') == 'no' and raw('calibrate.own.roas_after_lower') > raw('calibrate.own.roas_true') and raw('calibrate.bayes.roas_after_lower') > raw('calibrate.bayes.roas_true') and raw('geo.did.estimate') > raw('geo.truth'), 'that calibration moved both estimates toward the truth and narrowed both intervals past it') %}
Both estimates moved toward the truth, and both intervals narrowed until neither covers it: before
calibration each interval held the true return, and after it each sits wholly above it. The
