**Who to email.** Four policies were compared on the same customers: the T learner and the X
learner, uplift models that rank customers by how much the email changes their chance of buying;
the sure things rule, which emails the customers most likely to buy and is the rule most retailers
run; and everyone. The models were fit on {{ v('targeting.split.train') }} of customers; each policy
chose how many to contact on a {{ v('targeting.split.validation') }} validation split and is reported
on the {{ v('targeting.split.test') }} test split, which took no part in either. On test, per thousand
customers on the list, the T learner earned {{ v('targeting.hillstrom.t_learner.policy_value_test') }}
contacting {{ v('targeting.hillstrom.t_learner.chosen_share') }}, the X learner
{{ v('targeting.hillstrom.x_learner.policy_value_test') }} at {{ v('targeting.hillstrom.x_learner.chosen_share') }},
the sure things rule {{ v('targeting.hillstrom.sure_things.policy_value_test') }} at
{{ v('targeting.hillstrom.sure_things.chosen_share') }}, and emailing everyone
{{ v('targeting.hillstrom.everyone.policy_value_test') }}.
